<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>PROXY STATEMENT</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The board of directors (the &ldquo;<B>Board</B>&rdquo;) of Zhibao Technology
Inc. (the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;) is soliciting proxies for the extraordinary general meeting of shareholders (the &ldquo;<B>Meeting</B>&rdquo;)
of the Company to be held on September 29, 2026, at 9:00&nbsp;p.m., Beijing Time (September 29, 2026, at 9:00&nbsp;a.m. Eastern Time),
or any adjournment thereof. The Meeting&nbsp;will be held at Floor 3, Building 6, Wuxing Road, Lane 727, Pudong New Area, Shanghai, China,
201204 and virtually. Shareholders can participate in the Meeting, vote, and submit questions in person or via live webcast by visiting
http://www.virtualshareholdermeeting.com/ZBAO2026SM.</P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The notice of the Meeting, the proxy statement and the proxy card will
be made available to shareholders on or about September 9, 2026, These proxy materials contain instructions on how to access this proxy
statement online at:&nbsp;<I>www.proxyvote.com</I>, and how to submit your proxy to vote via the internet and/or mail.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>IMPORTANT: </B>Please
mark, date, and sign the enclosed proxy card and promptly return it in the accompanying postage-paid&nbsp;envelope or vote by telephone
or by Internet to assure that your shares are represented at the Meeting.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>RECORD DATE; VOTING POWER</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B><P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Only shareholders of the Company of record at
the close of business on September 1, 2026 (the &ldquo;<B>Record Date</B>&rdquo;) are entitled to attend and vote at the Meeting or at
any adjournment thereof. Quorum, for purposes of the Meeting, consists of at least one or more shareholders present or by proxy, or if
a corporation, by its duly authorized representative, representing not less than one-third of the issued and outstanding Class A ordinary
shares and Class B ordinary shares which are entitled to vote at such general meeting of the Company. As of the Record Date, there were
449,264,625 Class A ordinary shares and there were no Class B ordinary shares issued and outstanding, with each Class A ordinary shares
entitled to one vote per share and each Class B ordinary shares entitled to 20 votes per share.</P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>PROPOSALS TO BE VOTED ON</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">At the Meeting, the following proposals will be
considered and voted on:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Proposal&nbsp;No. 1 &mdash;&nbsp;The Share
Capital Increase Proposal</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;to approve, by ordinary resolution, the authorised share capital of the Company
be increased from US$50,000 divided into 500,000,000 ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001 each consisting of (i) 450,000,000
Class A ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001 each; and (ii) 50,000,000 Class B ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001
each, to US$200,000 divided into 2,000,000,000 ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001 each consisting of 1,950,000,000 Class A
ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001 each; and (ii) 50,000,000 Class B ordinary share with a par value of US$0.0001 each, by
the creation of 1,500,000,000 Class A ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001 each (the &ldquo;<B>Share Capital Increase</B>&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>



<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Proposal&nbsp;No. 2 &mdash; The Memorandum
and Articles Amendment No. 1 Proposal</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;by special resolution, subject to Proposal 1 above being passed at the
Meeting and upon effectiveness of the Share Capital Increase, to adopt an amended and restated memorandum and articles of association
to reflect, inter alia, the Share Capital Increase, the provision of veto rights over decisions of the Board to Botao Ma, and amendments
to permit a director to vote, and be counted in the quorum, on any matter in which he or she is interested subject to disclosure of that
interest (the &ldquo;<B>A&amp;R M&amp;A&rdquo;</B>).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Proposal&nbsp;No. 3 &mdash; The Share Consolidation
Proposal</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;to approve, by ordinary resolution, subject to the Share Capital Increase Proposal being passed at
the Meeting and the closing bid price on any trading day of the Company's Class A ordinary shares with a par value of US$0.0001 each listed
on Nasdaq Capital Market being below US$0.12 per share (&ldquo;<B>Trigger Event</B>&rdquo;), a consolidation of the Company&rsquo;s authorised,
issued and outstanding Class A ordinary shares and Class B ordinary shares of the Company (collectively, the &ldquo;<B>Shares</B>&rdquo;),
by consolidating each 50 Shares of the Company into 1 Share of the Company, with such consolidated Shares having the same rights and being
subject to the same restrictions (save as to nominal value) as the existing Shares of such class as set out in the A&amp;R M&amp;A (the
&ldquo;<B>Share Consolidation</B>&rdquo;), such Share Consolidation taking effect on the 15th trading day after the Trigger Event or such
later date as accepted by NASDAQ.</P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>Proposal&nbsp;No. 4 &mdash; The Memorandum and Articles Amendment
No. 2 Proposal:</B> by special resolution, subject to Proposal 3 above being passed at the Meeting and upon effectiveness of the Share
Consolidation, to adopt an amended and restated memorandum and articles of association to reflect the Share Consolidation (the &ldquo;<B>Further
M&amp;A</B>&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Proposal&nbsp;No. 5&nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;The Adjournment
Proposal</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;to approve, by ordinary resolution, the adjournment of the Meeting to a later date or dates or sine
die, if necessary or desirable, in the opinion of the directors, to permit further solicitation and vote of proxies if, at the time of
the Meeting, there are not sufficient votes for, or otherwise in connection with, the approval of the foregoing proposals.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>The Board recommends a vote &ldquo;FOR&rdquo;
each of the Proposals No.&nbsp;1-5.</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B></B></P>

